{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 44, :comments ["<b>And you shall sanctify yourselves and you shall be holy, etc.</b> Since our Sages of blessed memory said (Shabbat 104a) — one who comes to purify himself, they assist him; one who comes to defile himself, they open for him — but nevertheless they do not assist him. Therefore concerning one who comes to purify himself it says 'And you shall sanctify yourselves and you shall be holy' — by way of assurance, to say that if you begin to sanctify yourselves from below, then surely 'you shall be holy,' for I sanctify you from above and assist you in order that you be holy like Me, 'for holy am I.' But concerning one who comes to defile himself it says 'and you shall not defile yourselves in them, and you shall be made impure through them' — and it does not say 'and you shall be impure,' for this is not a certainty, for even though a person begins with corruption, nevertheless perhaps his deeds will not succeed, since they do not assist him from Heaven, but rather they open for him — for the door is open to him and none shuts against him. And by way of allusion it says 'וְנִטְמֵתֶם' missing an א, to tell you that the One (יחיד) of the world, blessed be He, departs from him, and He has no portion in his impurity, and his deeds have distanced Him."], :book :leviticus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:35:51.367302266Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}